<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australian Opp'n seeks to censure Costello.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australian Opp'n seeks to censure Costello.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's Labor Opposition moved in the House of Representatives on Tuesday to censure Treasurer Peter Costello for his alleged disclosure last week of a private briefing he had from U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan.</p>
<p>A censure motion is the strongest action that an opposition can take against a minister and is traditionally reserved for the most serious circumstances.</p>
<p>At 4.45 p.m. (0645 GMT) the debate was continuing and was expected to be lost on party lines.</p>
<p>-- Canberra Bureau 61-6 273-2730</p>
</text>
